From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: 977 - persist associated clients to sta table

The sta table existed since Phase 1 but nothing wrote it. Add mapc_sync_sta
(UPSERT keyed on macaddr, in the mapc_sync_bss style) + mapc_del_sta, driven
from the Phase-1 dispatcher on Topology Notification and Response. A roam
agent->agent rewrites the single row (macaddr PK); the row is deleted only on
a true disconnect (STA_DISCONNECTED branch). Makes clients visible in the DB
and the mesh-status WebUI, and persisted for recovery.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.h
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.h
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 struct node;
 struct netif_radio;
 struct netif_iface;
+struct sta;
 
 /* Upsert the single 'network' identity row (controller AL-MAC). */
 void mapc_sync_network(struct controller *c);
@@ -40,6 +41,13 @@
  * synced). No-op when the radio reports no BSS at all. */
 void mapc_sync_bss_sweep(struct controller *c, struct netif_radio *r);
 
+/* Upsert the 'sta' row for associated client @s (attached to node @n).
+ * Keyed on macaddr; a roam agent->agent rewrites the single row. */
+void mapc_sync_sta(struct controller *c, struct node *n, struct sta *s);
+
+/* Delete the 'sta' row for @s. Call ONLY on a true disconnect. */
+void mapc_del_sta(struct controller *c, struct sta *s);
+
 /* Rebuild the 'topology_link' edge set from c->topology.dev_list, one txn. */
 void mapc_sync_topology(struct controller *c);
 
